<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Illyrian Regions ~ Region Worksheet

''The sinking realm.'' Gaia's mythic Illyria mirrored: the Western-Balkan Adriatic coast and
its mountain wall, half-drowned since the Necrospire came down and ''still going under'' — the
impact that broke the world keeps pulling its landing-place beneath the sea, five centuries on.
Volcanic isles where mountains stood; hydrothermal vents where valleys ran; drowned temples
holding the traces of ancient gods.

''Strata of the realm:'' the ''Accursed Mountains'' inland (the Prokletije-mirror: Kollata, Maja
e Thatë, the ridges around the caldera) · the ''sinking coast'' (the archipelago of former
heights) · the ''drowned floor'' (temples, roads, and a realm's worth of sunken strata).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-caldera-region>>

!! The Caldera & the Spire

The impact crater rides the Accursed Mountains as a ''lava caldera with the Necrospire itself
as its central spire'' — the Pale Emperor's returned prison-ziggurat standing where it landed
(full canon: [[the-necrospire|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/concepts/the-necrospire]]). The Necrospire Cults guard
the rim, spreading necro-script corruption through the coastal settlements and calling the
realm's drowning a baptism.

''Prompts:'' what grows in a lava caldera five centuries old · which cult sect holds the rim
road this season · how close can a ship anchor before the necro-data storms read its rigging.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-realm>>

!! Powers, Strata, Hazards (gazetteer canon)

''Factions:'' the Necrospire Cults at the crater · ''Unseelie Raiders'' staging from sea-caves
and winter-bound isles · ''Independent Sea Clans'' — loose mariner confederations resisting
necromantic and fae control alike, often at odds with one another · ''Mobile Wain and Chariot
Clans'' running goods and warbands across causeways, tidal flats, and temporary land-bridges.

''The deep strata:'' warrior-mariner culture over drowned-city myth; Balkan tribal motifs with
Celtic/Gael connections — pre-Celtic, proto-Norse, Bell Beaker, Yamnaya, Etruscan, Basque —
old barrow cults, dead-route shrines, and sea-gate sanctuaries preserving ''extremely deep
divine strata'' beneath the later Greek, Thracian, and fae overlays. The oldest gods of the
Eastern Net sleep under this water.

''Position:'' west of the Olympian Marches (the corridor); the old ley-line hub connection
toward the Western Net; sea-routes toward the Hebros mouth.

''Hazards:'' unstable seafloor · undead armadas · boiling sea vents · fragile fae-clan
alliances · necro-data storms off the crater.

''Lares:'' severely damaged — partial memory loss, ghost-code contamination. A realm of nodes
that remember wrongly, which reads worse than not remembering at all.

''Prompts:'' which sea-clan would ferry a company toward the crater, at what price · what the
drowned temples' gods answer to now · where the Wain Clans' land-bridges actually go at the
lowest tide.

<<~/ahu>>

